# Pathfinder

Read `docs/PLAN.md` before implementing. Do the next unchecked step only, then mark that step done in the same change.

- TypeScript, React, and Node. One Render web service from the root Dockerfile. Listen on `0.0.0.0` and `process.env.PORT`. `GET /health` stays available.
- One secret: `MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN` in the repo-root `.env` (gitignored). The server reads it at runtime. The browser fetches the public token from the server. Do not add a second token variable, and do not log the token.
- No accounts. Stops and the round-trip toggle persist in `localStorage`.
- Mapbox Optimization API, profile `mapbox/driving`, or `mapbox/driving-traffic` when Consider current traffic is on. 2–12 stops. Round trip is a toolbar toggle (`roundtrip=true`, or `roundtrip=false` with `source=any` and `destination=any`).
- On load, restore the saved map center and zoom. If none was saved and stops exist, frame the stops. If there is no saved view and no stops, ask for the browser location. If that is denied or unavailable, center the map on Minsk (longitude 27.559, latitude 53.9006).
- Desktop first. The map fills the page. On a wide screen the upper-left toolbar keeps its width, rounded corners, and stays open. On a phone-sized screen at load, that toolbar is full width and collapsible. A centered caret stays visible at its bottom, pointing up while open and down while collapsed, and the header casts a shadow over that caret when the card is collapsed. The card eases open and closed. Map mode drops a draggable marker and keeps the stop being chosen visible, with Confirm and Remove. Confirming or removing it opens the toolbar again. After a route is drawn, the phone card collapses. Open in Yandex Maps then sends that visit order to the Yandex Maps app, then Yandex Navigator, then the Yandex Maps site. A round trip repeats the first stop at the end. On a phone the button stays visible while the card is collapsed, and it stays hidden while a place is being chosen on the map.
